Every game (SIL_HIDE_ON_DEACTIVATE=1): a fullscreen game hides itself when the player
switches to another (regular) app, as Wine does on Cmd-Tab with captured displays;
with SIL_DISPLAYMODE_RECORD (launch.sh's display mode hold) the desktop's own mode
(HiDPI) is back while the game is hidden, and the game's 1x mode when it returns.
While the player is in another app the program neither activates nor unhides itself
(Windows' foreground lock): no game pulls itself in front again after Cmd-Tab.
When the player comes back, the window that had the foreground is restored (if the
game minimized it) and gets the foreground back at once, in the game's own thread,
as a taskbar click does on Windows: the game takes clicks and keys again.
Apply after wine-winemac-reapply-gamma.patch.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
